    "image": "/guides/worlds-00.webp",
    "markdown": "# Crystal Journey: Seven Worlds of Meaning\n\nEveryone carries a private night sky inside them, and every so often the moonlight asks a quiet question: _who do I want to become?_ This crystal journey is an invitation to sit with that question and walk toward it one stone at a time.\n\nIf you are looking for a crystal guide for beginners, start here. Traditional belief holds that crystals carry the earth's steady, still energy. Worn or carried, they act less like teachers and more like a mirror, helping you notice your inner weather as you grow.\n\n## A Map of Seven Worlds\n\nTraditional belief describes seven chakras as doors into seven small worlds, each with its own colour and theme:\n\n  * **World 1 · Root** — red and black · grounding, safety, survival.\n  * **World 2 · Sacral** — orange · creativity, passion, emotional flow.\n  * **World 3 · Solar plexus** — yellow and gold · confidence, action, personal power.\n  * **World 4 · Heart** — green and pink · love, healing, acceptance.\n  * **World 5 · Throat** — blue · expression, truth, communication.\n  * **World 6 · Third eye** — indigo and violet · intuition, insight, wisdom.\n  * **World 7 · Crown** — white and clear · spirituality, connection, awakening.\n\n\n\n## Why Crystals Belong to Each World\n\nThree beliefs link a stone to its world: colour resonance (a crystal's colour is believed to echo its chakra's frequency), mineral memory (stones grown over millennia are said to hold steady energy), and companionship — a crystal mirrors your state rather than reshaping it.\n\n## How to Begin\n\n  * **Know yourself first.** Ask which feeling you carry most and which part of life you would soften.\n  * **Follow your instinct.** Notice which world pulls at you; intuition is often more honest than logic.\n  * **Begin lightly.** Choose one crystal, keep it close, and allow five quiet minutes a day. The moon sets its own pace; so may you.\n\n\n\n## Journey FAQs\n\n### What is the crystal journey?\n\nA traditional framework for self-exploration: seven chakra worlds, each paired with a family of crystals used for ritual and gentle reflection.\n\n### Which crystal world should I start with?\n\nThe one that speaks to you. Feeling unsteady? Begin in the root world. Longing for confidence? Visit the solar plexus world. Intuition is a more honest guide than logic.\n\n### Do I need a crystal from every world?\n\nNo. Many people keep a single stone for months. The journey has no quota and no deadline.\n\n### Is the crystal journey a medical treatment?\n\nNo. It is a traditional spiritual framework, and crystals are not medicine. For persistent physical or emotional discomfort, please speak with a healthcare professional.\n\n_The moon has already risen. Step into your first world and begin._"
