    "id": "connect-01",
    "series": "connect",
    "title": "Crystal Quiz: What Crystal Am I?",
    "eyebrow": "Begin the Connection",
    "excerpt": "Not sure what crystal am I? Take Lunar Talisman's crystal quiz — zodiac element, your need, and color intuition — to find your crystal match in minutes.",
    "color": "#ece7fb",
    "image": "/guides/connect-01.webp",
    "markdown": "# What Crystal Am I? Take the Crystal Quiz to Find Your Match\n\nThe right stone begins with an honest moment: admitting which part of you wants attention most. Lunar Talisman's crystal quiz is built around that moment — a short, instinct-driven conversation with yourself that ends in a recommendation you can actually wear.\n\nBefore you begin, let your shoulders drop. There are no wrong answers; choose the option that describes the you of right now, not the you you hope to become. Keep a piece of paper nearby and note your three answers — you will bring them to the guardian stone guide afterward.\n\n## How the Quiz Works: Three Questions\n\n### Question One · Your Zodiac Sign\n\nFind your sun sign and its element: **Fire** (Aries, Leo, Sagittarius), **Earth** (Taurus, Virgo, Capricorn), **Air** (Gemini, Libra, Aquarius), or **Water** (Cancer, Scorpio, Pisces). In crystal tradition, fire signs are paired with stones like garnet and sunstone, earth signs with citrine and tiger eye, air signs with clear quartz and amethyst, and water signs with moonstone and rose quartz. This answer plays a supporting role in your final match.\n\n### Question Two · The Area You Most Want to Improve\n\nChoose only one — the option that stirs you most and troubles you most:\n\n  * **A. Love and relationships** — warmer bonds, or a kinder relationship with yourself (rose quartz, strawberry quartz, pink quartz).\n  * **B. Career and wealth** — more focus, momentum, or financial ease (citrine, golden rutilated quartz, green phantom, tiger eye).\n  * **C. Health and vitality** — renewed energy, better sleep, a stronger body (garnet, red agate).\n  * **D. Inspiration and creativity** — unblocked ideas, expression, and passion (carnelian, sunstone).\n  * **E. Calm and rest** — less anxiety, deeper sleep (moonstone, amethyst, clear quartz).\n  * **F. Protection and cleansing** — a sense of safety, clearing heavy energy (obsidian, black rutilated quartz).\n\n\n\nThis answer carries the most weight in your result, because it names the real gap you are living with.\n\n### Question Three · The Color That Calls to You\n\nClose your eyes for three seconds, then open them and choose by first instinct: red, orange, yellow, green, pink, purple, blue, white, or black or brown. Color is the language your intuition speaks before your mind edits it — it confirms or refines the answers above. Red points to garnet or red agate; orange to carnelian or sunstone; yellow to citrine or tiger eye; green to green phantom; pink to rose quartz or strawberry quartz; purple to amethyst; blue to aquamarine or blue moonstone; white to clear quartz; and black or brown to obsidian or tiger eye.\n\n## Reading Your Result: An Example\n\nSay you are a Cancer (a water sign), your greatest wish is career growth (option B), and yellow keeps calling to you. Your **main stone** comes from row B — citrine — which happens to match your yellow instinct perfectly. Your **supporting stone** comes from your water-element row: moonstone. Two bracelets, one clear direction, nothing excessive.\n\nIf your three answers share no overlap, simply choose the stone from your improvement-goal row and keep it to one or two main pieces. A connection is built slowly; it is never measured by quantity. Quiz complete — now bring your answers to the guardian stone guide and meet your stones properly.\n\n_Still wondering what crystal am I? The quiz takes less than two minutes — answer honestly, note your three choices, and you will find your crystal match waiting for you in the guardian stone guide._"
