    "image": "/guides/crystals-00.webp",
    "markdown": "# The Crystal Encyclopedia: A Crystal Meanings Guide\n\nWelcome to the Lunar Talisman crystal encyclopedia — the map of the Codex, our library for crystals, the moon, and Eastern traditions. This guide does not promise miracle effects; it explains, in clear and quiet language, what traditional belief says about each stone, so your choice can rest on your own eye and heart.\n\nThe library holds eleven chapters; the color-series guides, chapters 02 to 06, form its heart. There, every stone appears by color family — traditional symbolism, chakra links where tradition pairs them, wearing notes, and cautions.\n\n## How to Use This Crystal Meanings Guide\n\n  * **New to crystals?** Read in order: 00 (this page) → 01 (chakras) → 02–06 (color series) → 07 (moon phases) → 08 (five elements) → 09 (zodiac) → 10 (FAQ).\n  * **Choosing by color?** Jump to whichever color series draws you first; each chapter stands alone.\n\n\n\n## Crystal Color Meanings at a Glance\n\nColor family| Traditional meaning| Chapter  \n---|---|---  \nRed & black| Courage, action, protection, cleansing| 02  \nOrange & yellow| Creativity, confidence, abundance| 03  \nGreen & pink| Heart healing, love, self-acceptance| 04  \nBlue & purple| Calm expression, wisdom, spirituality| 05  \nWhite & clear| Purity, cleansing, new beginnings| 06  \n  \n## Before You Begin Reading\n\n  * **Folklore, not science:** crystal energies, chakras, the five elements, and the zodiac belong to traditional culture, not scientific fact.\n  * **Careful wording:** every effect is written as traditional belief or is said to — never as a medical promise.\n  * **Health first:** this library offers no medical advice; please consult a doctor if you feel unwell.\n  * **Mindful buying:** quality and origin vary prices greatly; buy within your budget, and let the joy of wearing be the real reward.\n\n\n\n## Crystal Encyclopedia FAQs\n\n### Which chapter should I read first?\n\nStart with the color family you are drawn to. New readers often begin with chapter 06, the white and clear family — beginner favorites that pair easily with anything.\n\n### Does this encyclopedia claim that crystals heal?\n\nNo. Everything is presented as traditional belief and folklore, not medicine. For persistent discomfort, please see a doctor.\n\n### How do I find the stone that suits me?\n\nChapters 08 (five elements) and 09 (zodiac) match crystals to Eastern and Western traditions; chapter 10 answers the most common wearing questions.\n\n_Now choose the color that calls to you — the Codex will meet you there._"
