    "markdown": "# Crystal Care FAQ: Cleaning, Charging, and Wearing Your Stones\n\nCaring for a crystal is simpler than most guides make it sound. You need one safe cleaning method, a regular charging rhythm, and a few commonsense habits for daily wear. If you are still learning how to care for crystals, these are the questions we hear most, in the spirit of traditional belief rather than medical advice.\n\n## Cleaning and Charging Your Crystals\n\n### How often should I cleanse and recharge my crystal bracelet?\n\nA monthly cleanse on the full moon suits most daily-wear pieces and pairs naturally with full moon blessing batches. Cleanse sooner when the stone feels dull to you, and after intense experiences such as a hospital visit or a difficult emotional stretch.\n\n### What is the safest way to clean and charge crystals?\n\n**Moonlight is the gentlest and most versatile method:** place your bracelet on a windowsill or balcony around the full moon and let the moonlight fall on it overnight — it cleanses and recharges in one step. A **clear quartz cluster** works beautifully too: rest the stone on it for four to six hours. For hard stones, running water is fine, with three cautions:\n\n  * **Avoid salt water** for most stones — some minerals corrode or cloud.\n  * **Avoid harsh direct sun** — amethyst and pink quartz can fade.\n  * **Never use boiling water.**\n\n\n\n## Wearing and Everyday Care\n\n### Which hand should I wear my crystal bracelet on?\n\nThe traditional saying is **left in, right out**. The left hand is associated with receiving — love, luck, calm, and healing — so attracting and soothing stones are traditionally worn there. The right hand is associated with releasing and action, the traditional side for confidence, drive, and career stones. It is a custom, not a rule: whichever wrist feels right is the right one.\n\n### Can I wear more than one crystal at a time?\n\nYes — many collectors wear two or three pieces. A few gentle guidelines: keep each wrist to two or three bracelets so they do not crowd or rub; pair stones of similar hardness (soft stones should not press against hard ones); and stack same-direction energies rather than mixing energizing and calming stones on one wrist. One main stone for your primary intention, plus one or two supporters, is a balanced formula.\n\n### Should I shower, sleep, or exercise in my bracelet?\n\nRemove your bracelet before showering or bathing so soap residue does not clog the cord channel, and before exercise, where sweat and impacts dull the surface. Calming stones such as moonstone and amethyst may be worn to sleep or kept by your pillow. Apply lotion or perfume first, let it dry, then put your bracelet on.\n\n### What if my crystal bracelet breaks or I lose a stone?\n\nFolk tradition offers a tender reading: a crystal that breaks or goes missing is sometimes said to have absorbed what it could and completed its task. The customary response is to thank it and let it rest — bury it in the earth to return to nature, or rinse it and wrap it away in cloth. Physically, remember that crystals are natural minerals: a knock is ordinary wear, not a warning or a curse.\n\n### What if my crystal arrives damaged or does not feel right?\n\nBegin with the inspection step of the first-wear guide: check each bead and the cord, and photograph the bracelet in natural light on arrival. If anything looks wrong — a chipped bead, broken cord, or detail that does not match your certificate — contact our customer service team with your order number and photos, and they will confirm the next steps for your situation, whether a replacement or a return.\n\n## Choosing and Understanding Your Stones\n\n### How do I know if my crystal is real?\n\nUse common sense and good channels: natural stone feels cool at first and warms slowly, rarely shows neat round bubbles, and resists scratches from a key or blade. Natural inclusions — wisps, internal fractures, color zoning — are a sign of authenticity, while suspicious perfection at a bargain price is the real red flag. High-value pieces deserve an independent certificate, and our full moon batches carry an energy activation certificate you can verify.\n\n### How quickly will I notice a difference with my crystal?\n\nTraditional belief describes a settling-in period of days to weeks, and noticing nothing at first is entirely normal. More practically, the value of a crystal lives in what it reminds you to do — wear it as a prompt to be calm, focused, or brave, and the habit itself carries the change. Crystals are companions and gentle reminders, not medicine; they are not a substitute for professional medical, psychological, or financial care.\n\n_Care is simply attention made routine: cleanse with the moon, wear with intention, and your stones will stay bright for years._"
